    "body": "## Security impact\n\nPrivate job-publication records contain pre-publication financial state such as wallet reservation and online payment amounts. The authenticated read/cancel/payment-preparation paths previously loaded a publication globally by numeric id and only then rejected a non-owner with 403, while a nonexistent id returned 404. That allowed authenticated users to enumerate whether private publication ids exist.\n\n## Fix\n\n- add a pessimistically locked owner-scoped publication lookup `(publicationId, userId)`;\n- use that lookup for `GET /job-publications/{id}` and cancellation;\n- use the same owner-scoped lookup before preparing Stripe PaymentIntent creation;\n- return the existing neutral `ResourceNotFoundException` for non-owners and missing ids;\n- keep internal provider/webhook/recovery lookups global because those ids come from trusted durable system state;\n- preserve normal owner behavior and financial reservation semantics.\n\n## Tests\n\n- outsider cannot enumerate a publication through read;\n- outsider cannot enumerate or trigger wallet restoration through cancellation;\n- outsider cannot enumerate or start Stripe PaymentIntent preparation;\n- owner read/payment preparation/cancellation behavior remains covered.\n\nNo schema changes.",
